; expect 42
; A name that a global declaration occupies must not capture every
; call with that spelling. `let` bindings and function parameters
; shadow it, and every consumer of the frontend has to agree that this
; program is accepted AND that it computes 42.
;
; THIS FILE REPLACES `010-trait-scope`, which pinned the same
; property through a trait method name. Traits are gone; the property
; is not. `isBuiltinName`, `isMacroName` and `isEffectName` are the
; occupants the resolver still asks about at one place in
; `typecheck.ax`, and an effect OPERATION is the one a program can
; declare for itself - so it is what this file uses. Measured before
; it was written: the operation `sz` below is never invoked as an
; operation, so no handler is needed and AX3053 does not arise; every
; `sz` here resolves to the binding that shadows it.
(effect Sz (
  sz :: (-> Int Int)
))

(:: viaParam (-> (-> Int Int) Int))

(fn (viaParam sz) (sz 5))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (if (==
    (+
      (let ((sz 
        (lambda (q) 7)
      ))
        (sz 5)
      )      (viaParam
        (lambda (q) 7)
      )
    )    14
  )
    42
    1
  )
)
